# The JVM sbt itself runs in, for okay2's own build (okay2-cross). Until
# okay2 crossed to Scala.js and Native it ran on the launcher's default
# heap; with the JS linker and the Native tooling of twelve more projects
# in the same process, the core's 100 000-cell test died of
# "OutOfMemoryError: Java heap space" inside sbt — the root build's
# .jvmopts says why a shared heap fails that way, and this is its answer.
-Xmx6g
-Xss8m
-XX:MaxMetaspaceSize=1g
